WEBVTT

00:29.112 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.867
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.868 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:43.043 --> 00:46.045
ETA
1 HOUR

00:46.046 --> 00:47.172
One hour.

01:21.790 --> 01:23.125
BEN

01:24.835 --> 01:27.295
Hey, Ben. I'm driving.

01:27.296 --> 01:30.172
-  Do you have your passport?
- My passport? Uh…

01:30.173 --> 01:33.134
It's in my room, in the third drawer. Why?

01:33.135 --> 01:35.678
Get your passport
and come to the airport.

01:35.679 --> 01:37.555
We have to go to the States right now.

01:37.556 --> 01:39.932
What? What are you saying?

01:42.102 --> 01:43.812
Why do we have to go?

01:44.521 --> 01:46.231
Come to my office.

01:50.277 --> 01:54.572
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

01:54.573 --> 01:55.656
EPISODE 6

01:59.619 --> 02:01.078
Hello?

02:01.079 --> 02:02.163
Express delivery?

02:02.164 --> 02:03.748
I'll head there right away.

02:03.749 --> 02:07.460
Ben, I just got here.
I'm going to receive my passport.

02:07.461 --> 02:10.671
Hurry. There aren't many seats left
for the 7:30 flight.

02:22.017 --> 02:24.310
- Hey.
-  Hurry up! We don't have time.

02:24.311 --> 02:25.479
I'm heading inside now.

02:26.021 --> 02:27.147
Okay.

02:32.402 --> 02:35.572
HANG IN THERE!

02:37.282 --> 02:39.993
Hello. This way, please.

02:41.953 --> 02:43.246
DESIGNER SONG HARAN

02:45.749 --> 02:47.458
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

02:47.459 --> 02:50.795
Dear passengers,
this is Korea Air, Flight 202

02:50.796 --> 02:53.298
headed for Los Angeles
International Airport.

02:53.799 --> 02:55.633
Please wear your seatbelts

02:55.634 --> 02:59.887
and switch all electronic devices
to airplane mode.

03:04.142 --> 03:05.602
MISSED CALL
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

03:07.270 --> 03:09.563
Mr. Park, did you hear from Mr. Seonu?

03:09.564 --> 03:10.565
Oh?

03:12.943 --> 03:17.363
He said he'd take
the earliest flight to the US.

03:17.364 --> 03:18.949
He must be gone already.

03:22.828 --> 03:24.830
YOUR PHOTOS ARE READY FOR PICKUP.
HOBAK PHOTO STUDIO

03:25.872 --> 03:27.916
The project's suspended?

03:28.834 --> 03:30.292
Producer Ben said

03:30.293 --> 03:33.295
there were major executive changes
at the US headquarters.

03:33.296 --> 03:38.008
And the new decision-maker said
they'll halt all ongoing projects.

03:38.009 --> 03:40.428
The project's up in the air right now.

04:02.492 --> 04:05.161
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

04:05.162 --> 04:06.912
They really left?

04:06.913 --> 04:08.122
The entire staff?

04:08.123 --> 04:11.083
The production team left in a hurry
after hearing the news.

04:11.084 --> 04:13.002
I'll share any updates if I receive any.

04:13.003 --> 04:15.255
This is just so sudden.

04:17.549 --> 04:20.509
All animation work
will be on hold for now.

04:20.510 --> 04:23.345
We'll start meetings
for the next season tomorrow,

04:23.346 --> 04:24.681
so get ready.

04:25.265 --> 04:26.390
Team 1 meeting's over.

04:26.391 --> 04:28.142
- Call Team 2.
- All right.

04:28.143 --> 04:30.854
-  Thank you.
- Thank you.

04:39.362 --> 04:41.822
Wow. Weren't we pretty close?

04:41.823 --> 04:43.824
He could've at least sent a message.

04:43.825 --> 04:45.743
His phone's off, too.

04:45.744 --> 04:48.078
He was using
a temporary phone here, right?

04:48.079 --> 04:50.165
Pureum, he's not using
this number in the States?

04:51.249 --> 04:54.001
- Chan isn't coming here anymore, then?
-  Hmm…

04:54.002 --> 04:56.170
I feel like he'll come back soon, though.

04:56.171 --> 04:58.339
Why? Did he tell you something?

04:58.340 --> 04:59.548
No,

04:59.549 --> 05:02.928
but I feel like he'll solve everything
and come back soon.

05:03.637 --> 05:07.723
Chan doesn't seem like the type
to just end things like this.

05:07.724 --> 05:10.769
Right. It hasn't been confirmed
that it's canceled yet.

05:11.686 --> 05:13.980
Chan might already be pretty close

05:14.606 --> 05:16.607
to the new person in charge.

05:16.608 --> 05:20.778
You're right. He'll solve it straight away
and return with a surprise.

05:20.779 --> 05:23.405
What kind of surprise?

05:23.406 --> 05:25.617
For example…

05:28.703 --> 05:30.997
What's this huge box? Fabric samples?

05:31.665 --> 05:33.833
The Chan you ordered is here!

05:36.795 --> 05:37.878
Ta-da!

05:37.879 --> 05:40.464
He could appear like a magic trick.

05:40.465 --> 05:42.091
That's possible.

05:42.092 --> 05:44.302
That does suit him.

05:46.263 --> 05:50.016
Seonu Chan really is something.
He's making us laugh even when he's away.

05:50.684 --> 05:52.560
Geez.

05:52.561 --> 05:53.978
I really miss him.

06:04.573 --> 06:05.906
Hmm…

06:07.242 --> 06:10.203
A reinterpretation
of Nana Atelier's early outfits.

06:12.539 --> 06:14.874
Oh, my. This is going to work.

06:14.875 --> 06:16.459
The new Haran's killing it lately.

06:17.168 --> 06:20.212
You have digital files
of videos from the '70s, right?

06:20.213 --> 06:21.839
I'll share them with you now.

06:21.840 --> 06:23.091
Ah.

06:24.134 --> 06:28.346
Okay. Then let's build on that
and do some more research…

06:29.806 --> 06:30.807
Tsk.

06:31.725 --> 06:36.854
I'm sure Chan will come back
in a few days, saying "Surprise!"

06:36.855 --> 06:38.397
So…  Don't worry.

06:38.398 --> 06:41.109
But if he contacts you
before then, tell us right away.

06:42.235 --> 06:44.988
- What?
- Wouldn't he contact you first?

06:45.864 --> 06:47.865
You haven't been screening your windows.

06:47.866 --> 06:50.035
I know it's because of Chan.

06:50.785 --> 06:52.369
I'm very perceptive, you know.

06:55.707 --> 06:57.291
Hello?

06:57.292 --> 06:58.500
New Haran?

06:58.501 --> 06:59.836
It's mine.

07:00.253 --> 07:01.337
Yes, Ms. Kim.

07:01.338 --> 07:04.049
I was going to visit on the weekend.

07:05.091 --> 07:07.302
My phone doesn't seem to be ringing…

07:20.357 --> 07:21.399
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

07:24.194 --> 07:25.527
LOS ANGELES TIME DIFFERENCE

07:25.528 --> 07:27.237
SEOUL IS 17 HOURS AHEAD OF LOS ANGELES

07:27.238 --> 07:29.323
It would be morning there.

07:29.324 --> 07:31.076
HAVE YOU ARRIVED YET?

07:50.512 --> 07:51.554
Darn it.

07:52.514 --> 07:53.598
Did I fall asleep here?

07:54.432 --> 07:55.600
What time is it?

07:56.601 --> 07:58.811
I must be crazy.

08:23.670 --> 08:25.462
Innovative materials?

08:25.463 --> 08:27.131
You mean using new materials?

08:27.132 --> 08:31.094
Yes. The same beauty,
but more eco-friendly.

08:31.720 --> 08:35.639
We'll recreate
one of our archive's 1979 silk pleated set

08:35.640 --> 08:37.933
with fermented protein fabric.

08:37.934 --> 08:41.438
It'll be eco-friendly
and maintain its elegant mood.

08:42.021 --> 08:45.065
Nice. Maison has been using
new materials these days, too.

08:45.066 --> 08:48.194
We could target eco-conscious consumers
who don't buy clothes.

08:48.778 --> 08:50.196
That's what I mean.

08:50.822 --> 08:51.989
We can't.

08:51.990 --> 08:56.535
Nana Atelier built its name
on silk and cashmere craftsmanship.

08:56.536 --> 08:58.579
Using unstable, unverified materials

08:58.580 --> 09:01.749
may jeopardize our launch schedule
as well as brand trust.

09:01.750 --> 09:04.793
The show is meant to showcase
the brand's vision.

09:04.794 --> 09:07.921
Young consumers care about
both style and sustainability.

09:07.922 --> 09:09.673
We should adapt to the times.

09:09.674 --> 09:11.425
It's all about
value-based consumption now.

09:11.426 --> 09:13.135
If we don't, we'll get discarded.

09:13.136 --> 09:15.387
Customer trust comes first for our brand.

09:15.388 --> 09:17.556
Moving away from our premium materials

09:17.557 --> 09:20.184
will risk losing the loyalty
of our longtime customers.

09:20.185 --> 09:23.312
I know trust is important,
but the world has changed.

09:23.313 --> 09:26.440
A brand that doesn't change
is even more risky.

09:26.441 --> 09:28.193
Taking a risk is more dangerous.

09:28.777 --> 09:30.444
We already have a packed schedule.

09:30.445 --> 09:34.364
It won't be wise to make a risky move
that may disrupt our timeline.

09:34.365 --> 09:35.575
- I--
-  Stop.

09:36.409 --> 09:38.453
I welcome
discussions like this anytime.

09:39.204 --> 09:42.831
Let's put some more thought into this
and discuss it again next time.

09:42.832 --> 09:44.334
- Yes, ma'am.
- Okay.

09:44.959 --> 09:46.043
I prepared everything.

09:46.044 --> 09:49.506
There's something else.
I received good news this morning.

09:53.927 --> 09:55.720
What? Do you want to perform or something?

09:57.222 --> 09:58.388
Oh…

09:58.389 --> 10:01.601
No, I just needed to adjust my outfit.

10:03.228 --> 10:05.521
The pre-order stock
for the Lafayette coats

10:05.522 --> 10:07.856
have already sold out.

10:07.857 --> 10:09.733
We received additional orders.

10:09.734 --> 10:11.026
That's amazing!

10:11.027 --> 10:12.820
That's great news.

10:12.821 --> 10:15.906
Good. Make sure everything stays on track
until they're shipped.

10:15.907 --> 10:17.242
Yes, ma'am.

10:21.412 --> 10:23.957
Hey. Was I wrong?

10:24.541 --> 10:26.542
Using materials
that didn't exist back then

10:26.543 --> 10:27.876
is what we call reinterpretation.

10:27.877 --> 10:29.169
You're right.

10:29.170 --> 10:31.004
The fermented protein fabric idea
was good.

10:31.005 --> 10:32.756
Then why was Mr. Yeon like that?

10:32.757 --> 10:35.968
"No. Customer trust comes first."

10:35.969 --> 10:38.095
"We can't risk customer loyalty."

10:40.431 --> 10:41.515
What?

10:47.856 --> 10:50.190
Here's the list of outfits
for tomorrow's VIP fitting.

10:50.191 --> 10:51.651
Please get everything ready.

10:55.488 --> 10:58.783
It's my job to bridge the gap
between the artist's vision and reality.

11:01.911 --> 11:05.832
He cares so much about our family,
but why is he so strict with me?

11:06.374 --> 11:08.418
I'm not bothered at all.

11:13.256 --> 11:15.258
She seems incredibly bothered, right?

11:16.050 --> 11:17.218
Totally.

11:17.802 --> 11:20.512
But aren't disagreements like that
common during meetings?

11:20.513 --> 11:23.932
That's what I mean.
Why is she suddenly so upset?

11:23.933 --> 11:25.601
I don't understand the reason.

11:25.602 --> 11:26.603
The reason…

11:27.353 --> 11:28.688
Hmm.

11:37.363 --> 11:42.744
I'm sure Chan will come back
in a few days, saying "Surprise!"

11:44.162 --> 11:45.662
When did you get here?

11:45.663 --> 11:47.206
You should've called.

11:47.207 --> 11:48.916
Did everything go okay?

11:51.544 --> 11:52.754
Excuse me?

11:53.713 --> 11:56.549
Oh… Sorry, I mistook you for someone else.

12:04.849 --> 12:06.892
Am I sleep deprived?

12:06.893 --> 12:09.561
WAITING FOR GODOT

12:13.066 --> 12:15.526
Hello.

12:16.402 --> 12:18.070
Hey, you're here.

12:18.071 --> 12:20.530
Is Genius still not eating?

12:21.616 --> 12:23.868
He doesn't seem to have
an appetite either.

12:24.452 --> 12:26.704
- Sit. I'll make you coffee.
- Okay.

12:34.587 --> 12:35.588
Huh?

12:36.506 --> 12:39.132
You're not sitting
in your seat of seven years?

12:39.133 --> 12:41.678
I want to sit here today.

12:51.104 --> 12:52.522
It feels like there's a hole.

12:54.107 --> 12:58.486
My heart feels so empty.
It's like wind is blowing through it.

13:00.196 --> 13:04.284
I feel like he'll burst in any second,
shouting "Mr. Park!"

13:05.118 --> 13:08.496
and going on and on about something.

13:12.792 --> 13:13.875
Mr. Park!

13:15.211 --> 13:16.462
Did you have fun? Huh?

13:17.255 --> 13:18.798
Genius. Hey.

13:32.145 --> 13:34.896
You forgot your meds again, didn't you?

13:34.897 --> 13:37.400
I really need to scold you.

13:38.943 --> 13:42.779
I feel like I'll start hearing him
nag me again.

13:42.780 --> 13:45.240
- When will he come back?
- Oh?

13:45.241 --> 13:46.701
What? Is he here?

13:48.703 --> 13:49.828
Donggu.

13:49.829 --> 13:51.288
Hello.

13:51.289 --> 13:54.499
Is Chan still not back from Gyeongju?

13:54.500 --> 13:56.084
I can't reach him.

13:56.085 --> 13:57.461
He went to the US.

13:57.462 --> 13:58.713
What?

14:28.951 --> 14:29.994
Hadam!

14:32.121 --> 14:34.706
Don't you usually go
to the study lounge on this day?

14:34.707 --> 14:35.999
Yes.

14:36.000 --> 14:39.878
It's so nice to ride a swing
after such a long time.

14:39.879 --> 14:42.673
How did you get any free time?

14:44.342 --> 14:46.260
I have something to ask you.

14:48.930 --> 14:50.639
CHA YOUGYUM

14:53.851 --> 14:55.227
It's grated yam.

14:55.228 --> 14:57.687
I did some research,
and they said it helps.

14:59.649 --> 15:03.110
Why was your tumbler
in my grandma's study?

15:03.111 --> 15:04.402
Huh?

15:04.403 --> 15:05.696
Oh… Well…

15:06.197 --> 15:08.866
I ran into her a while ago in the park.

15:09.700 --> 15:13.203
I left my tumbler behind,
and I guess she kept it for me.

15:13.204 --> 15:15.289
Grandma lied and said it was hers.

15:19.919 --> 15:22.255
You keep bringing up my grandma
for no reason,

15:23.089 --> 15:25.216
and you've been behaving strangely
these days.

15:26.259 --> 15:27.343
What was first?

15:28.010 --> 15:29.554
My grandma?

15:32.348 --> 15:33.349
Or Han Sora?

15:34.308 --> 15:35.309
What?

15:35.810 --> 15:37.687
Why are you suddenly mentioning Han Sora?

15:40.231 --> 15:43.401
Park Yeseul…
Why did she have to bring up Han Sora?

15:44.360 --> 15:45.735
Should I give him a snack?

15:49.782 --> 15:51.908
SORA

15:53.911 --> 15:55.829
Hey, Yougyum. It's me, Han Sora.

15:55.830 --> 15:57.706
What are you doing after practice?

15:57.707 --> 15:58.958
What about you?

16:01.002 --> 16:04.087
Her number was saved on your phone
with a heart.

16:04.088 --> 16:05.922
She just saved it without asking.

16:05.923 --> 16:08.425
I only found out the day she saved it.

16:08.426 --> 16:09.677
So you did meet her.

16:10.219 --> 16:11.220
Well…

16:12.930 --> 16:15.891
I did, but I actually…

16:17.101 --> 16:18.560
Hadam, it wasn't like that.

16:18.561 --> 16:20.562
She kept following me when I told her--

16:20.563 --> 16:22.397
"You're too young to marry."

16:22.398 --> 16:23.982
"Quit the nonsense."

16:23.983 --> 16:27.235
Did Grandma summon you
and threaten you or something?

16:27.236 --> 16:30.030
Why would you say that?
You know she wouldn't do such a thing.

16:30.031 --> 16:31.865
You and Grandma both deceived me.

16:31.866 --> 16:33.658
What are you hiding from me?

16:33.659 --> 16:36.870
Did she throw water at you,
telling you not to disrupt my studies?

16:36.871 --> 16:39.122
Did you get annoyed
and decide to meet Han Sora?

16:39.123 --> 16:40.333
Don't say that!

16:42.043 --> 16:44.211
Don't you know your own grandma?

16:44.212 --> 16:46.380
- Don't you know me?
- I don't!

16:52.094 --> 16:54.554
I met her to try to win
some brownie points,

16:54.555 --> 16:56.807
and I met Han Sora
to tell her I'm marrying you

16:57.683 --> 16:59.517
and that I'll report her as a stalker.

16:59.518 --> 17:01.478
I told her to get lost.

17:01.479 --> 17:04.148
That's all I said.
I only spoke to her for one minute.

17:05.107 --> 17:07.442
It's nothing like what you think--

17:07.443 --> 17:08.569
No.

17:09.153 --> 17:10.279
I don't believe you.

17:11.572 --> 17:14.616
I just can't believe
that you hid something from me.

17:16.244 --> 17:17.744
You feel like a stranger to me.

17:17.745 --> 17:20.122
What are you talking about?

17:22.250 --> 17:23.251
Fine.

17:23.918 --> 17:26.879
I couldn't tell you,
but that was only because of one thing.

17:29.173 --> 17:30.466
I was afraid you'd get hurt.

17:31.884 --> 17:32.885
But how…

17:37.473 --> 17:38.557
Why are you crying?

17:38.558 --> 17:40.475
I'm the one who should be crying.

17:40.476 --> 17:42.687
Did I not mean anything to you?

17:43.271 --> 17:44.772
It's you and me, Hadam.

17:45.523 --> 17:48.233
- This is just something trivial--
- Trivial?

17:48.234 --> 17:49.985
Is this trivial to you?

17:49.986 --> 17:51.486
No, Hadam. I didn't mean--

17:51.487 --> 17:52.862
If you were me…

17:54.365 --> 17:57.951
If people were gossiping
about me seeing another guy,

17:57.952 --> 18:00.620
then you see his name
saved with a heart on my phone,

18:00.621 --> 18:02.498
and I keep hiding things from you…

18:03.666 --> 18:05.334
- Then wouldn't you--
- No.

18:06.252 --> 18:08.462
No matter what people say about you,

18:09.589 --> 18:12.383
I only trust what I've seen
and the Hadam I know.

18:13.593 --> 18:14.719
That's the difference…

18:18.180 --> 18:19.181
between you and me.

18:22.018 --> 18:24.186
I'm sorry,
but I can't walk you home today.

18:35.531 --> 18:36.866
Ms. Song!

18:46.584 --> 18:47.792
Oh…

18:47.793 --> 18:49.377
It's you, Mr. Yeon.

18:49.378 --> 18:50.503
Pardon?

18:50.504 --> 18:51.588
It's nothing.

18:51.589 --> 18:53.758
I just reported this to Ms. Kim,

18:54.508 --> 18:56.719
but I got an email a moment ago

18:57.511 --> 18:58.596
from Producer Ben.

19:03.434 --> 19:05.769
All the other projects
have been canceled,

19:05.770 --> 19:08.313
and it's not looking good
for Ben's team either.

19:08.314 --> 19:10.690
Seeing how he asked
to halt the collaboration,

19:10.691 --> 19:12.777
it'll be difficult to resume the project.

19:13.819 --> 19:15.696
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

19:17.448 --> 19:20.241
The number you have dialed is unavailable.

19:20.242 --> 19:21.744
Please leave your message--

19:24.288 --> 19:26.122
You can use me as a friend
when you're bored

19:26.123 --> 19:27.791
or a misunderstanding for Ms. Kim.

19:27.792 --> 19:29.502
Just try me out as a free trial.

19:30.086 --> 19:33.129
As soon as the three months is over,

19:33.130 --> 19:34.715
I'll disappear without a trace.

19:39.387 --> 19:42.264
What kind of trial
ends so suddenly like this?

19:50.815 --> 19:52.691
What was that look Mr. Yeon gave me?

19:52.692 --> 19:54.776
He's so warm and friendly
to everyone else.

19:54.777 --> 19:56.487
Why is he so cold to me?

20:05.579 --> 20:07.373
Everything's a mess already,

20:07.873 --> 20:09.166
and now our house, too?

20:10.042 --> 20:11.334
Song Hayeong.

20:11.335 --> 20:12.711
I almost slipped on this.

20:12.712 --> 20:16.089
What? You didn't fall.

20:16.090 --> 20:19.426
-  Just clean this up.
- I'll clean it later.

20:19.427 --> 20:21.261
Just go do your thing.

20:21.262 --> 20:22.721
When is "later"?

20:22.722 --> 20:24.889
It's always when someone
cleans up after you.

20:24.890 --> 20:27.600
Always? Why would you say that?

20:27.601 --> 20:29.853
Do you think
I never clean up after myself?

20:29.854 --> 20:33.648
Stop being childish
and clean up your own mess.

20:33.649 --> 20:35.442
Yes, ma'am.

20:35.443 --> 20:36.943
Song Hayeong.

20:36.944 --> 20:39.989
I'm taking a short nap,
so please be quiet.

20:40.656 --> 20:42.532
I'm coming back in five minutes,
so clean this.

20:42.533 --> 20:44.617
I said I'll clean it later.

20:44.618 --> 20:45.953
You didn't even fall down.

20:47.913 --> 20:48.956
What did you just say?

20:52.251 --> 20:54.378
Yougyum, let's talk…

20:59.300 --> 21:00.675
Say that again.

21:00.676 --> 21:03.094
It's okay if I didn't fall down?

21:03.095 --> 21:05.513
Why are you taking
your anger out on me?

21:05.514 --> 21:07.265
Go take it out
on the person who upset you.

21:07.266 --> 21:08.683
Why are you picking a fight?

21:08.684 --> 21:10.351
You're the one who caused it.

21:10.352 --> 21:13.313
You clearly caused this,
and I'm the victim here.

21:13.314 --> 21:15.356
If you're so logical,
you should've been a lawyer.

21:15.357 --> 21:17.609
- Why did you become a designer?
- Hey!

21:17.610 --> 21:19.652
You two are so childish.

21:19.653 --> 21:21.529
Haven't you two aged at all?

21:21.530 --> 21:23.823
Can't you be quiet for 30 minutes?

21:23.824 --> 21:25.492
If you want to fight, go downstairs.

21:25.493 --> 21:27.368
You sleep downstairs.

21:27.369 --> 21:28.745
Being a high school senior
isn't everything.

21:28.746 --> 21:31.289
When did you ever show
any consideration for me?

21:31.290 --> 21:34.043
You never did anything
to help me with my studies!

21:34.543 --> 21:36.461
Forget it.

21:36.462 --> 21:38.963
What would I expect
from such immature people?

21:38.964 --> 21:40.673
There's no point talking to you.

21:44.178 --> 21:45.386
Song Hadam!

21:45.387 --> 21:47.764
You shouldn't be so mean
just because you're angry.

21:47.765 --> 21:50.099
Then why were you so mean to me?

21:50.100 --> 21:51.101
You…

21:52.144 --> 21:55.272
Forget it. Just clean this up.

22:01.487 --> 22:02.613
Did you just…

22:04.615 --> 22:05.908
- throw that at me?
-  Ah.

22:06.492 --> 22:07.742
Sorry.

22:07.743 --> 22:10.578
I was trying to clean it up,
but my hand slipped.

22:10.579 --> 22:12.039
If you're so upset, throw it back.

22:14.208 --> 22:15.917
I threw it like you said.

22:15.918 --> 22:18.711
You're not the only one
who can be stubborn, you know.

22:18.712 --> 22:21.130
That's not being stubborn.
It's being crazy.

22:24.260 --> 22:25.760
- Hey!
- What?

22:25.761 --> 22:27.054
You…

22:46.115 --> 22:47.908
What am I even doing?

23:00.880 --> 23:01.881
You cleaned it up.

23:02.464 --> 23:03.465
Yes.

23:05.467 --> 23:07.844
Are you… going somewhere?

23:07.845 --> 23:10.222
Yes, I'm going there.

23:11.348 --> 23:12.724
What's with the car key?

23:12.725 --> 23:13.976
I was about to go there, too.

23:15.394 --> 23:16.770
Should we go together?

23:17.646 --> 23:18.772
Fine.

23:19.607 --> 23:20.774
But just us?

23:21.859 --> 23:25.653
E raised to the power of 3in
equals negative c plus one.

23:25.654 --> 23:28.239
So for both sides to be equal,

23:28.240 --> 23:30.575
c should be 0, and d should be 1.

23:30.576 --> 23:33.661
Then hx to the power of x is negative 2…

23:33.662 --> 23:36.164
We're going to go there.

23:36.165 --> 23:37.707
If you want to join…

23:37.708 --> 23:43.671
Applying this formula
would give you x squared minus 2x plus 1.

23:43.672 --> 23:45.423
Did you get that?

23:45.424 --> 23:46.674
And…

24:00.022 --> 24:01.690
There are people passing by.

24:02.191 --> 24:04.025
It's so pretty.

24:04.026 --> 24:06.195
The ocean's beautiful.

24:15.913 --> 24:18.706
- I ended things with Yougyum.
- Huh?

24:18.707 --> 24:19.874
- What?
- Why?

24:19.875 --> 24:21.502
Should we try talking to him?

24:22.628 --> 24:24.922
We never argued before,

24:25.506 --> 24:27.840
but we cried and shouted at each other.

24:27.841 --> 24:30.511
So I can't even focus on studying.

24:31.512 --> 24:35.056
At this rate,
I'll mess up on the CSAT as well.

24:35.057 --> 24:38.017
My life is ruined.

24:40.521 --> 24:43.773
Did you just laugh? This is serious.

24:43.774 --> 24:47.443
I'm facing the biggest crisis
of my life right now.

24:47.444 --> 24:51.031
My gosh. Arguing with your boyfriend twice
might destroy the entire planet.

24:53.325 --> 24:55.410
You were acting like a grown-up,

24:55.411 --> 24:57.328
- but I guess you're still a baby.
- Hey.

24:57.329 --> 24:58.622
What did you two argue about?

25:00.582 --> 25:03.377
There was
a small misunderstanding…

25:04.003 --> 25:06.213
It's obvious
that it was your fault.

25:06.755 --> 25:08.423
He did something wrong, too.

25:08.424 --> 25:12.010
You should've seen his face.
How could he look at me like that?

25:13.554 --> 25:16.890
And, Hayeong,
what were you so pissed about?

25:19.935 --> 25:21.145
I don't know.

25:22.021 --> 25:24.355
It wasn't even anything serious.

25:24.356 --> 25:25.649
Why did I get so upset?

25:26.483 --> 25:27.567
It's a mystery.

25:27.568 --> 25:28.901
What?

25:28.902 --> 25:31.155
I know. It's weird.

25:31.822 --> 25:33.949
Anyway, I'm fine now.

25:34.742 --> 25:36.117
So it's a pass.

25:36.118 --> 25:37.702
What about you, then?

25:37.703 --> 25:41.080
What made you
throw snacks at me like that?

25:41.081 --> 25:43.792
What? She threw snacks at you?

25:44.752 --> 25:47.003
I missed a fun event.

25:47.004 --> 25:51.049
"Everything's a mess already."
Weren't you talking about yourself?

25:51.050 --> 25:53.843
I guess I just felt a bit upset.

25:53.844 --> 25:56.054
What's going on? Huh?

25:56.055 --> 25:57.472
What is it?

25:57.473 --> 25:58.974
It's just…

25:59.808 --> 26:02.435
My spring picnic ended too early.

26:02.436 --> 26:04.979
Geez. What are you saying?

26:04.980 --> 26:07.315
I hate it when people talk in riddles.

26:07.316 --> 26:08.525
Just be straightforward…

26:11.987 --> 26:12.988
It's cold.

26:13.572 --> 26:15.407
I should stick close to you for a bit.

26:16.241 --> 26:17.533
Let's go if you're cold.

26:17.534 --> 26:19.369
No, I want to stay a bit longer.

26:20.746 --> 26:23.664
Why is it so cold?

26:41.058 --> 26:42.768
Are you sure you're all right?

26:43.352 --> 26:44.560
Me?

26:44.561 --> 26:45.978
I'm fine.

26:45.979 --> 26:47.647
I'm always fine.

26:47.648 --> 26:50.233
I should be asking you that. Are you okay?

26:50.234 --> 26:51.235
Yes.

26:52.069 --> 26:53.112
I'll be fine.

26:54.029 --> 26:55.656
And I want to be fine.

26:57.241 --> 26:58.992
So I'm going to be okay.

27:00.160 --> 27:03.705
All right. I hope you will.

27:04.832 --> 27:08.627
Oh. I actually liked it
when we fought, though.

27:09.253 --> 27:10.587
It reminded me of old times.

27:13.841 --> 27:15.467
Chan's a really good guy.

27:16.510 --> 27:17.593
Huh?

27:17.594 --> 27:20.472
You'd normally never drink
on a business trip.

27:21.682 --> 27:24.434
So I asked Raemee
about what happened in Gyeongju.

27:26.144 --> 27:29.146
I'm sure Chan will get in touch soon.

27:30.357 --> 27:31.525
So let's just wait.

27:37.573 --> 27:39.449
It's called an iridescent cloud.

27:40.409 --> 27:43.871
They say you have good luck
if you see an iridescent cloud.

27:44.872 --> 27:49.750
You should look for iridescent clouds
in the sky, too,

27:49.751 --> 27:51.252
instead of just vapor trails.

27:58.844 --> 28:00.762
I guess that was fake, too.

28:02.306 --> 28:03.599
ADD NEW WALLPAPER

28:20.198 --> 28:21.408
It's okay.

28:22.492 --> 28:23.910
Good morning.

28:23.911 --> 28:25.578
It's not a good morning.

28:25.579 --> 28:26.996
Our animation collaboration--

28:26.997 --> 28:29.249
I heard. It's too bad.

28:29.917 --> 28:32.627
Je Raemee, can we do the concept meeting?

28:32.628 --> 28:33.961
Huh?

28:33.962 --> 28:35.046
Sure.

28:35.047 --> 28:36.590
Then let's begin in 10 minutes.

28:42.471 --> 28:44.680
"It's too bad"?

28:44.681 --> 28:45.891
That's it?

28:47.601 --> 28:51.020
We even went on a trip
to Gyeongju together.

28:51.021 --> 28:52.773
Doesn't she feel upset?

28:53.398 --> 28:54.482
ARCHIVES

28:54.483 --> 28:56.651
You must have cleaned out the archives.

28:56.652 --> 28:57.903
When did you find all this?

28:58.403 --> 28:59.904
I came pretty early today.

28:59.905 --> 29:03.282
I was looking through the material, and…

29:03.283 --> 29:04.575
You can take it.

29:04.576 --> 29:05.702
Sorry.

29:06.828 --> 29:08.913
Hmm? It's not mine.

29:08.914 --> 29:10.332
Oh.

29:12.042 --> 29:13.293
It's just spam.

29:14.211 --> 29:17.254
Anyway,
although this is a reinterpretation,

29:17.255 --> 29:18.798
I'd like a fresh twist…

29:18.799 --> 29:21.217
One, you're really okay.

29:21.218 --> 29:24.053
Two, you're pretending to be okay.

29:24.054 --> 29:26.514
Which is it?
You're not even checking your phone.

29:26.515 --> 29:27.640
You two were close--

29:27.641 --> 29:30.351
Why wouldn't I be okay?
We haven't known each other long.

29:30.352 --> 29:32.353
You're as cold as dry ice.

29:32.354 --> 29:34.356
You're so cold.

29:35.023 --> 29:37.484
I take back the 3.5 points.
You're zero points.

29:38.527 --> 29:41.487
Anyway, if you look at these photos,

29:41.488 --> 29:44.573
they seem pretty fresh even though
they're from 40 to 50 years ago.

29:44.574 --> 29:47.368
So instead of struggling
to create something new…

29:52.541 --> 29:54.291
Hi.

29:54.292 --> 29:56.585
Hey. Come and sit.

29:56.586 --> 29:58.046
- Do you want some coffee?
- Yes.

29:59.256 --> 30:01.174
You're not sitting by the window?

30:01.466 --> 30:03.301
This is my usual seat.

30:04.052 --> 30:06.555
Wait, was I acting like I own this place?

30:07.431 --> 30:11.600
By the way, it seems like the project
we were doing will be canceled.

30:11.601 --> 30:13.645
Then Chan won't come back?

30:14.896 --> 30:16.022
Probably not.

30:16.023 --> 30:18.567
I thought I should tell you
since you've been waiting.

30:19.901 --> 30:21.278
Then he could've told me…

30:31.538 --> 30:33.331
CALCULUS

30:37.044 --> 30:39.879
Wow. I've never seen Yougyum
wearing glasses before.

30:39.880 --> 30:40.963
He looks so good.

30:40.964 --> 30:43.592
-  Right?
-  He's so handsome.

30:46.303 --> 30:49.388
I only trust what I've seen
and the Hadam I know.

30:49.389 --> 30:51.724
That's the difference between you and me.

30:51.725 --> 30:53.225
He's so handsome.

30:53.226 --> 30:55.144
I can't believe it.

30:55.145 --> 30:56.562
I wish I could date him.

30:56.563 --> 30:58.315
Gosh, I'm so into him.

31:00.233 --> 31:01.817
Has his eyesight gotten bad?

31:01.818 --> 31:04.279
It'll be uncomfortable
playing with glasses on.

31:06.907 --> 31:09.034
What does it matter? We broke up anyway.

31:15.874 --> 31:19.418
Here's the operations report
you asked for last time.

31:19.419 --> 31:20.754
You're done already?

31:24.508 --> 31:25.591
Ah.

31:25.592 --> 31:28.094
It's too bad
the animation project got canceled.

31:28.095 --> 31:31.305
I'm actually glad
I can focus more on our next season.

31:31.306 --> 31:33.308
Call me if there's anything else you need.

32:00.544 --> 32:02.920
Should we bring the curve down
another 0.3 mm?

32:02.921 --> 32:06.924
And I think we should lower the neckline
by 0.5 mm as well.

32:06.925 --> 32:08.093
Then along the V-neck…

32:10.345 --> 32:11.471
What is this?

32:17.185 --> 32:18.353
It's so funny.

32:21.314 --> 32:24.234
The number you have dialed
is unavailable. Please leave--

32:24.818 --> 32:26.153
It's still turned off.

32:26.987 --> 32:29.196
She didn't even come to work.
Where is she?

32:29.197 --> 32:32.533
Isn't she in the storage room?
She's been going there before work.

32:32.534 --> 32:34.160
Her bag's not in her office.

32:34.161 --> 32:35.412
I don't think she even came here.

32:36.246 --> 32:38.123
Oh? She sent an email.

32:40.167 --> 32:42.793
"I'm sorry. I have to take a day off,

32:42.794 --> 32:45.671
so I'm sharing what I was planning
to cover in our meeting."

32:45.672 --> 32:49.300
What? Has she ever taken a day off before?

32:49.301 --> 32:51.177
Why didn't she keep her phone on?

32:51.178 --> 32:53.554
It's like she was determined to go AWOL.

32:53.555 --> 32:54.556
Go AWOL…

33:00.061 --> 33:01.437
Ms. Kim, Haran…

33:01.438 --> 33:02.772
Knock!

33:04.482 --> 33:06.984
Ms. Kim, why did Haran
suddenly take a day off?

33:06.985 --> 33:09.654
She has the right to take a day off.
Is there a problem?

33:10.238 --> 33:14.283
No,
but I think there's something wrong…

33:14.284 --> 33:18.078
I'm not sure, but it was strange
how she threw those snacks.

33:18.079 --> 33:19.246
And she said something

33:19.247 --> 33:21.916
about her picnic ending
and everything being a mess.

33:21.917 --> 33:23.876
You're the one who seems like a mess.

33:23.877 --> 33:25.753
What I mean is…

33:25.754 --> 33:27.756
Aren't you worried about her, Grandma?

33:28.715 --> 33:29.716
No.

33:30.217 --> 33:32.176
She's not a kid. She'll be fine.

33:32.177 --> 33:33.887
Go. Don't bother me.

33:35.388 --> 33:38.892
Where the heck is she?

33:47.651 --> 33:50.028
Your daughter's growing up, isn't she?

33:52.656 --> 33:54.241
LEAVE REQUEST FORM
SONG HARAN

34:01.873 --> 34:03.041
Hello.

34:04.167 --> 34:05.585
I'll be there on time.

34:07.003 --> 34:09.047
Yes,
we're scheduled to ship today.

34:09.673 --> 34:12.008
If the Lafayette customers respond well…

34:21.601 --> 34:24.353
You've been
to the dementia care center,

34:24.354 --> 34:26.438
- so we'll start with a screening test.
- Okay.

34:26.439 --> 34:28.066
Don't you have
a guardian with you?

34:30.151 --> 34:31.360
No.

34:31.361 --> 34:32.987
We'll call you when it's your turn.

34:32.988 --> 34:33.989
All right.

34:39.911 --> 34:42.496
What? If this isn't urgent--

34:42.497 --> 34:45.541
Didn't you confirm the Brulee Coat
as a one-button?

34:45.542 --> 34:47.543
Yes, a one-button. Why?

34:47.544 --> 34:50.587
The QC report for the factory
was stamped as a pass,

34:50.588 --> 34:52.840
but there's no button in the sample.

34:52.841 --> 34:55.010
We have less than four hours left
before shipment.

34:56.594 --> 35:00.140
Contact the Seongsu-dong factory.
I'll be there soon.

35:02.225 --> 35:03.768
How did I make such a mistake?

35:07.022 --> 35:09.941
SUNYUL NATIONAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

35:12.152 --> 35:13.444
Ms. Kim Nabong!

35:13.445 --> 35:14.738
Wait, Na…

35:15.488 --> 35:17.656
Ms. Kim Nabong?

35:17.657 --> 35:18.825
Nabong!

35:26.708 --> 35:27.709
Nabong!

35:28.335 --> 35:29.336
Nabong!

35:34.591 --> 35:35.592
What…

35:36.301 --> 35:37.636
What was she doing here?

35:39.638 --> 35:41.013
How much time do we have?

35:41.014 --> 35:42.097
Two hours.

35:42.098 --> 35:44.309
This won't work.
We should negotiate postponing--

35:45.477 --> 35:46.978
No, I'm not negotiating anything.

35:47.729 --> 35:50.689
If I can't keep our promises,
then I'm not fit to make clothes.

35:50.690 --> 35:53.567
I mistook it for a no-button coat,
so I'll fix this.

35:56.905 --> 35:59.240
We're adding buttons to all 70 coats.

36:00.158 --> 36:01.867
Bring them when they're done.

36:01.868 --> 36:03.995
I'll be checking each piece myself.

36:14.005 --> 36:15.256
-  Pass.
-  Pass.

36:18.051 --> 36:19.052
Again.

36:20.303 --> 36:21.304
Pass. Pass.

36:23.765 --> 36:26.267
We have
an hour and 10 minutes until shipment.

36:34.693 --> 36:35.902
Thank you.

36:38.363 --> 36:40.948
The shipment to Paris
has just been loaded.

36:42.409 --> 36:43.867
- What a relief.
- We did it.

36:43.868 --> 36:45.160
I'm so glad.

36:56.005 --> 36:57.089
I'm sorry.

36:57.090 --> 36:59.883
I made you work twice
because of my mistake.

36:59.884 --> 37:02.512
If it weren't for you,
we wouldn't have made them on time.

37:03.096 --> 37:04.514
Great job, everyone.

37:13.690 --> 37:15.150
I'm sorry. It was my mistake.

37:16.317 --> 37:18.610
I should have checked it
before the final sample.

37:18.611 --> 37:21.072
That's enough. It was clearly my mistake.

37:21.614 --> 37:25.826
And don't tell the design team about this.
There's no need to alarm them.

37:25.827 --> 37:27.078
Yes, ma'am.

37:27.579 --> 37:28.746
I'll drive you home.

37:30.582 --> 37:31.750
It's fine.

37:32.250 --> 37:34.001
Treat the factory workers to a meal…

37:34.002 --> 37:36.254
I booked a restaurant
and gave them expenses.

37:37.255 --> 37:38.256
I'd like

37:39.090 --> 37:40.967
to take you home today.

37:43.052 --> 37:44.596
I just want to walk for a bit.

37:45.263 --> 37:46.347
You can go.

38:11.623 --> 38:15.585
Whatever it is, I don't want you
to bear everything on your own.

38:16.336 --> 38:18.254
You can tell me anything, Ms. Kim.

38:46.783 --> 38:50.662
Hey, Hadam. Is Haran home?
She didn't call either?

38:52.664 --> 38:56.626
I'm on my way home,
but there's a lot of traffic…

38:59.420 --> 39:00.504
Huh?

39:00.505 --> 39:01.923
Hang on.

39:09.180 --> 39:10.598
Was I mistaken?

39:24.362 --> 39:26.489
Huh? Why are they sleeping here?

39:27.115 --> 39:28.324
Shh.

39:31.619 --> 39:33.788
They passed out
while waiting for you.

39:34.747 --> 39:37.125
So I was the culprit.

39:42.422 --> 39:44.757
It's late. Go and get some sleep.

39:46.718 --> 39:47.760
Good night.

39:54.142 --> 39:55.602
But why aren't you asking

39:56.311 --> 39:59.313
why I took the day off
or what I did all day?

39:59.314 --> 40:00.607
You're here, so it's fine.

40:01.190 --> 40:03.401
But next time,
write a proper form when taking a leave.

40:04.944 --> 40:06.362
It's not an art class, you know.

40:07.155 --> 40:09.364
Don't scribble on the request form.

40:09.365 --> 40:11.450
It wasn't a joke…

40:11.451 --> 40:12.869
A butterfly knot.

40:14.037 --> 40:16.164
You needed time to get some closure…

40:16.998 --> 40:18.416
on Seonu Chan.

40:20.460 --> 40:23.086
Normally, you'd never
go on a business trip a day early.

40:23.087 --> 40:26.215
And the expressions on your face
in the videos…

40:27.550 --> 40:30.762
I guess… you grew more attached to him
than I thought,

40:31.429 --> 40:33.389
seeing how you needed time for closure.

40:36.100 --> 40:37.101
I just…

40:37.894 --> 40:40.104
wanted to be okay.

40:43.191 --> 40:45.485
When we first met, he told me

40:46.778 --> 40:50.239
that it seemed like
I was trapped in winter.

40:51.574 --> 40:52.699
Thank you.

40:52.700 --> 40:53.951
-  Thank you for these.
-  Enjoy.

40:53.952 --> 40:55.119
Thank you.

40:58.998 --> 41:02.084
Don't you crave croissants
when you see the crescent moon?

41:02.085 --> 41:06.297
I didn't want to get trapped
in winter again, so I wanted to be okay,

41:06.923 --> 41:09.258
but it didn't go well.

41:11.636 --> 41:13.261
I forgot to buy this.

41:13.262 --> 41:15.097
It's my favorite.

41:15.098 --> 41:16.349
Take this.

41:17.767 --> 41:19.644
Whatever I do, whatever I see,

41:20.728 --> 41:22.438
I keep getting reminded of him.

41:23.231 --> 41:25.857
There are 0.3, 0.4, 5, 6,

41:25.858 --> 41:28.653
oil-based, water-based,
nib tip, and ballpoint pens.

41:30.154 --> 41:32.239
SEONU CHAN

41:33.700 --> 41:38.246
I couldn't figure out
a way to be okay,

41:39.414 --> 41:40.915
but then I found this.

41:41.916 --> 41:43.542
SEOUL DESTINATIONS LIST

41:43.543 --> 41:45.753
Choose where to go first
so we can go together later.

41:47.005 --> 41:50.967
So I thought I'd have some closure
if I checked off the whole list.

41:51.592 --> 41:56.430
This could be the final knot.

41:56.431 --> 41:57.681
-  What about this?
-  This?

41:57.682 --> 42:00.018
-  Can I try this?
-  It looks good on you.

42:01.519 --> 42:03.771
How should I choose?

42:08.234 --> 42:11.111
Sorry, but could you take a photo of us?

42:12.196 --> 42:13.280
- We'll take one for you, too.
- Thank you.

42:13.281 --> 42:14.573
Oh, I'm okay.

42:14.574 --> 42:15.742
Thank you.

42:17.035 --> 42:19.661
So I went sightseeing
here and there

42:19.662 --> 42:21.913
and tried a lot of things…

42:31.632 --> 42:34.719
But I kept feeling bored, for some reason.

42:35.970 --> 42:41.559
Everything I did with him
was just so fun and exciting,

42:42.435 --> 42:45.521
so I thought it would be fun
to do whatever was on the list.

42:48.399 --> 42:49.525
Haran.

42:51.235 --> 42:55.155
People, relationships, and even memories

42:55.156 --> 42:58.993
could disappear tomorrow
if you let them slip through your hands.

42:59.994 --> 43:01.913
Go to the US and see him.

43:02.497 --> 43:05.123
Whether you become okay or not,
get it sorted.

43:05.124 --> 43:07.210
You can easily meet him if you want to.

43:08.419 --> 43:12.547
No, we were never that close
to begin with.

43:12.548 --> 43:13.757
That would be silly.

43:13.758 --> 43:19.555
There's nothing as sad and stupid
as regretting things

43:20.431 --> 43:22.224
after time has passed.

43:22.225 --> 43:25.228
Life is too short
to spend it on regretting things.

43:26.270 --> 43:28.815
He was going to go back anyway.

43:29.440 --> 43:31.025
He just left earlier than planned.

43:33.611 --> 43:36.238
This is why I didn't want
to get close to anyone.

43:36.239 --> 43:37.573
So do you regret it?

43:39.117 --> 43:42.578
Do you regret getting to know Mr. Seonu?

43:45.623 --> 43:46.666
I do…

43:48.042 --> 43:49.168
have regrets.

43:50.586 --> 43:52.547
If I knew he'd leave so quickly,

43:53.131 --> 43:54.340
I would have been…

43:56.342 --> 43:57.467
kinder to him.

44:00.429 --> 44:02.932
I was a bit mean to him at first.

44:04.433 --> 44:07.186
But I don't regret

44:08.563 --> 44:09.939
getting to know him.

44:10.523 --> 44:11.815
A three-month trial!

44:11.816 --> 44:13.233
There's nothing to lose.

44:13.234 --> 44:15.026
You can overcome it.

44:15.027 --> 44:16.696
Once you know how,

44:17.488 --> 44:19.782
you'll be able to escape on your own.

44:20.491 --> 44:25.454
I learned it through that person,
so I wanted to show you, too.

44:26.038 --> 44:27.957
Thanks to that weird trial,

44:29.375 --> 44:31.711
I learned how to escape on my own.

44:34.714 --> 44:37.425
So I know I met a great person.

44:40.428 --> 44:42.013
I feel grateful.

44:44.599 --> 44:46.809
Then that's enough.

45:03.868 --> 45:07.163
Traditional knots
each have a specific meaning.

45:08.331 --> 45:11.208
A new life, change…

45:11.209 --> 45:14.836
Sometimes, you have to free something
instead of clutching it tightly

45:14.837 --> 45:16.505
to open up a new beginning.

45:17.173 --> 45:20.384
That's what… this butterfly knot means.

45:34.315 --> 45:36.525
Is she not coming today either?

45:37.526 --> 45:40.320
Sorry, I'm late.
It took some time picking up bribes.

45:40.321 --> 45:41.988
- She's here.
- Ms. Song.

45:41.989 --> 45:44.157
I was late helping her carry this.

45:46.410 --> 45:48.912
This is an apology
for taking a leave without notice.

45:48.913 --> 45:51.373
-  Thanks.
-  Thank you.

45:51.374 --> 45:52.750
Didn't you bring mine?

45:53.334 --> 45:54.960
Of course, we did.

45:56.671 --> 45:59.924
Someone go visit Mr. Yoon's exhibit later.
I have plans today.

46:00.383 --> 46:01.384
I'll go.

46:04.011 --> 46:06.347
All right. Go and visit him.

46:07.556 --> 46:09.225
- Thanks for the coffee.
- Sure.

46:12.353 --> 46:14.354
-  Thank you.
-  Thank you.

46:14.355 --> 46:15.772
Drop by when you're free.

46:15.773 --> 46:17.733
There's another thing
waiting for its owner.

46:24.991 --> 46:25.992
Yes?

46:27.410 --> 46:29.703
I'll go with you.

46:29.704 --> 46:32.539
I thought you'd return
to your cold, distant self.

46:32.540 --> 46:33.708
I'm proud of you.

46:40.965 --> 46:42.008
Here.

46:42.967 --> 46:44.467
What is it this time?

46:44.468 --> 46:46.887
Did you find a flower ring
you were going to give me?

46:48.597 --> 46:51.183
I saw you when I was getting my checkup.

46:53.936 --> 46:55.437
Why were you at the hospital?

46:55.438 --> 46:56.938
Are you sick or anything?

46:56.939 --> 46:59.858
I was just visiting a friend there.

46:59.859 --> 47:03.195
Then what made you rush out like that?
You even dropped your hat.

47:04.572 --> 47:08.617
Something urgent came up at work,
so, of course, I wasn't skipping happily.

47:11.787 --> 47:13.121
Oh, right.

47:13.122 --> 47:15.458
Seonu Chan
didn't contact you either, did he?

47:16.125 --> 47:17.126
What?

47:18.210 --> 47:21.922
No, he didn't.
I'm actually worried about Haran, though.

47:22.631 --> 47:25.216
There seemed to be something
going on between them.

47:25.217 --> 47:28.721
I'm worried she'll end up in pain
like seven years ago.

47:29.305 --> 47:30.722
It won't happen again.

47:30.723 --> 47:33.351
She seems to have grown stronger
after spending time with him.

47:33.934 --> 47:37.146
Right. My roommate
was quite an incredible guy.

47:39.565 --> 47:40.900
I feel really grateful.

47:41.484 --> 47:42.943
It's such a shame.

47:49.283 --> 47:51.160
I loved the exhibit.

47:52.370 --> 47:53.953
Gosh, look at all these people.

47:53.954 --> 47:57.457
Being out here on a bustling street
makes me so excited!

48:03.798 --> 48:05.757
7:00 P.M. SAMCHEONG-DONG
TODAY 7:00 P.M.

48:05.758 --> 48:08.009
Ah. Mark that on your schedule.

48:08.010 --> 48:09.845
You'd better not forget or show up late.

48:13.557 --> 48:15.183
I totally forgot about this.

48:15.184 --> 48:17.019
Can't I cancel it?

48:19.647 --> 48:20.730
Oh, God!

48:20.731 --> 48:23.149
Isn't this restaurant
so, so, so famous

48:23.150 --> 48:27.029
that you have to wait for months
to book a table?

48:28.197 --> 48:29.657
Take me instead of canceling.

48:30.408 --> 48:32.450
There isn't much time left…

48:32.451 --> 48:34.119
It's just right over there.

48:34.120 --> 48:36.287
We can get there if we run.

48:36.288 --> 48:38.624
Come on!

48:44.630 --> 48:45.631
This is amazing.

48:46.924 --> 48:48.925
It's so nice and peaceful here.

48:57.560 --> 48:58.561
Yes, Ms. Kim.

48:59.228 --> 49:00.771
Yes, I saw him.

49:02.314 --> 49:04.691
I took a pamphlet, too.

49:07.153 --> 49:08.154
All right.

49:08.988 --> 49:10.114
Hello?

49:10.990 --> 49:12.658
Really? Okay.

49:14.452 --> 49:16.411
I'm really sorry.

49:16.412 --> 49:20.123
My partner's a soldier,
and he just got an unexpected leave.

49:20.124 --> 49:23.209
- So, I'm sorry, but I have to go.
- What?

49:23.210 --> 49:24.461
Enjoy your meal. Bye.

49:24.462 --> 49:25.962
I'm very sorry!

49:25.963 --> 49:27.714
What…

49:27.715 --> 49:29.091
Wait, your scarf…

49:29.717 --> 49:30.967
Je Raemee!

49:30.968 --> 49:32.802
Wait!

49:32.803 --> 49:35.221
Je Raemee, here!

49:35.222 --> 49:36.306
Your scarf…

49:36.307 --> 49:37.892
Give it to me next time.
Sorry!

49:41.979 --> 49:44.190
-  I'm sorry.
- It's okay, I'll do it.

49:44.857 --> 49:46.442
- Sorry.
- No problem.

49:54.450 --> 49:55.951
Why did I even come here?

50:09.632 --> 50:11.759
It's even snowing?

50:20.643 --> 50:21.852
Ms. Song!

50:26.440 --> 50:27.650
Hearing things again?

50:32.404 --> 50:33.447
Ms. Song!

51:03.143 --> 51:04.353
How have you been?

51:09.191 --> 51:11.610
I told you not to be late, but I'm late.

51:14.113 --> 51:16.240
Oh? Why do you look so frail?

51:17.199 --> 51:18.993
Did you not eat well?

51:19.827 --> 51:21.161
Has work been tough?

51:25.291 --> 51:27.418
Um… Well…

51:27.960 --> 51:29.460
Aren't you happy to see me?

51:29.461 --> 51:31.297
I'm so happy that I almost hugged…

51:34.049 --> 51:35.133
I mean…

51:36.802 --> 51:39.137
I almost did a backflip.

51:42.182 --> 51:43.766
Here. How about a high five instead?

51:43.767 --> 51:46.395
I usually do high fives
when I'm happy to see someone.

52:10.628 --> 52:12.212
I have a habit…

52:13.422 --> 52:15.257
of hugging people I'm happy to see.

52:34.526 --> 52:39.031
I promised that I'd be here by today,
no matter what.

52:54.546 --> 52:56.964
You messaged me? When?

52:56.965 --> 52:59.718
Didn't you come here
because of my message?

53:02.221 --> 53:04.430
Please wear your seatbelts

53:04.431 --> 53:08.268
and switch all electronic devices
to airplane mode.

53:10.521 --> 53:11.604
I'll be back soon.

53:11.605 --> 53:13.815
Even if the project gets canceled,
I'll be back soon.

53:13.816 --> 53:15.692
We said we'd have dinner together.

53:15.693 --> 53:16.984
I promise to be there by that day.

53:16.985 --> 53:18.736
Don't worry even if you can't reach me.

53:18.737 --> 53:20.988
Tell Mr. Park and everyone not to worry.

53:20.989 --> 53:22.448
Sir, we'll be taking off soon.

53:22.449 --> 53:24.325
- Please switch to airplane mode.
- Okay.

53:28.497 --> 53:30.832
It's on.

53:30.833 --> 53:31.834
Oh.

53:32.793 --> 53:33.960
Look, I sent it…

53:33.961 --> 53:36.463
Oh? What's this exclamation mark?

53:39.133 --> 53:41.009
It means it failed to send.

53:42.553 --> 53:46.597
Oh! If you didn't receive
my message, then you must have…

53:46.598 --> 53:49.101
You're here, so it's fine. Eat up.

53:56.150 --> 53:57.401
Have more of this.

54:02.656 --> 54:04.199
Here.

54:05.826 --> 54:07.243
Eat all of that, okay?

54:07.244 --> 54:09.036
This is why you're so thin.

54:09.037 --> 54:12.708
Are there no mirrors in the States?
You're the one who looks so gaunt.

54:13.292 --> 54:16.128
I should've dressed up a bit.

54:16.795 --> 54:18.296
It's been a while since we met.

54:20.841 --> 54:22.383
What about headquarters?

54:22.384 --> 54:24.720
Mr. Yeon said it's not looking so good.

54:25.345 --> 54:26.555
Oh, um…

54:27.973 --> 54:30.934
I'm not sure
how to tell you this,

54:31.894 --> 54:33.771
- but…
- It got canceled, right?

54:34.521 --> 54:36.940
Then do you have to go back soon?

54:38.108 --> 54:41.236
This is really important, so…

54:45.073 --> 54:47.993
I resolved everything really well.

54:54.333 --> 54:56.501
It's me, Seonu Chan.

54:56.502 --> 54:58.503
We've already visited the site.

54:58.504 --> 55:00.004
Seeing it in person, it's clear

55:00.005 --> 55:02.381
we can take this project
beyond the original idea.

55:02.382 --> 55:05.259
If anything needs adjusting,
we can move on it right away.

55:05.260 --> 55:06.719
No.

55:06.720 --> 55:09.640
It almost got canceled, but…

55:10.557 --> 55:13.976
I think Scene 27 feels
a bit flat. What do you think?

55:13.977 --> 55:17.271
I don't think it's about the sharpness,
it's about the keyframe timing.

55:17.272 --> 55:20.650
I don't think it's about impact.
The emotion isn't just coming through.

55:20.651 --> 55:23.819
Emergency meetings, back-to-back meetings,

55:23.820 --> 55:26.198
persuasion, even script revisions…

55:27.866 --> 55:30.577
Hey, uh…
how's the background coming along?

55:31.662 --> 55:35.331
Around 60 percent. But they want
another look at the main character.

55:35.332 --> 55:36.791
- At this point?
-  Yeah.

55:45.008 --> 55:46.092
Thank you.

55:48.512 --> 55:49.888
Yeah?

55:50.889 --> 55:53.140
Okay. We'll be right there.

55:53.141 --> 55:54.768
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

55:55.978 --> 55:58.563
Hey, they're asking for a script meeting.
Okay? Come on.

55:58.564 --> 56:00.439
We didn't want to give up, no matter what,

56:00.440 --> 56:04.235
so we all fought through it
with gritted teeth.

56:04.236 --> 56:07.280
We agreed to revise the parts
that had differing opinions.

56:07.281 --> 56:09.824
That's such a relief.

56:09.825 --> 56:11.784
You said you worked on it
for over two years.

56:11.785 --> 56:13.452
That's one thing…

56:13.453 --> 56:14.454
Mmm…

56:16.373 --> 56:18.959
But I really wanted to apply Won's costume

56:19.543 --> 56:22.754
that you made in the animation.

56:23.922 --> 56:27.134
And that's what got me through it.

56:32.806 --> 56:35.850
Let's eat up and go.
Mr. Park's been waiting for you.

56:35.851 --> 56:37.936
I want to spend more time with you.

56:39.354 --> 56:40.939
Can you stay out late tonight?

56:48.363 --> 56:50.740
I'll clear the table
and bring your dessert.

56:50.741 --> 56:51.824
Thank you.

56:51.825 --> 56:54.535
I should call Mr. Park.

56:59.291 --> 57:00.458
Mr. Park, I'm here.

57:00.459 --> 57:03.377
Genius, Chan is here!

57:03.378 --> 57:05.255
- Why are you crying?
- He's crying?

57:06.548 --> 57:08.341
I'm sorry I couldn't call.

57:08.342 --> 57:10.384
No, no. It's fine.

57:10.385 --> 57:13.137
I'm just so happy.

57:13.138 --> 57:15.223
I thought I'd never see you again.

57:15.974 --> 57:18.017
I was so upset.

57:18.018 --> 57:19.894
Don't cry.

57:19.895 --> 57:22.272
Now I can finally sleep easy.

57:25.901 --> 57:27.069
Yes.

57:28.862 --> 57:30.906
Yes. All right.

57:35.202 --> 57:38.038
Make sure to have dinner
and take your meds. I'll visit later.

57:38.664 --> 57:39.665
Okay.

57:41.458 --> 57:42.793
He was so excited, wasn't he?

57:44.336 --> 57:48.214
Mr. Park and the others
were waiting for you the whole time.

57:48.215 --> 57:53.427
Our whole team, Genius,
and even Donggu came looking for you.

57:53.428 --> 57:56.723
I'm so glad everything worked out.

57:57.432 --> 57:59.975
Only good things
will happen from now on.

57:59.976 --> 58:00.977
For real.

58:02.145 --> 58:04.856
Everything's going to be fine now.

58:05.524 --> 58:06.858
Everything's fine.

58:33.260 --> 58:34.761
JAY YOON 2ND EXHIBIT

58:42.269 --> 58:45.939
I missed you too,
but Haran would've had quite a hard time.

58:46.690 --> 58:49.108
You're the one
who gave her the camera, right?

58:49.109 --> 58:53.404
She seemed so excited
when she was taking the photos,

58:53.405 --> 58:56.240
but after you left,
her eyes were always bloodshot

58:56.241 --> 58:58.785
as if she wasn't sleeping well.

59:26.646 --> 59:29.815
We'll do this line.

59:29.816 --> 59:31.192
Please send us an email.

59:31.193 --> 59:32.194
All right.

59:32.861 --> 59:35.571
But is business not going well these days?

59:35.572 --> 59:36.947
Our company?

59:36.948 --> 59:41.827
Mr. Yeon came by in person yesterday,
so I wondered if anything's wrong.

59:41.828 --> 59:45.039
Why would he come here in person?

59:45.040 --> 59:47.458
He always paid upfront
when placing orders,

59:47.459 --> 59:50.085
but this time, he asked to pay afterward,

59:50.086 --> 59:52.171
saying he needed new materials.

59:52.172 --> 59:53.465
New materials…

59:54.883 --> 59:56.759
- Was it…
- Bio-silk.

59:56.760 --> 59:58.053
Fermented protein fabric.

01:00:01.848 --> 01:00:05.893
He said he didn't want money
to limit the designers' creativity.

01:00:05.894 --> 01:00:09.104
He asked us to get the material,
no matter what.

01:00:09.105 --> 01:00:10.856
It's been 10 years,

01:00:10.857 --> 01:00:13.318
but I've never seen him
ask for something so earnestly.

01:00:16.613 --> 01:00:20.075
- Mr. Yeon, where are you?
-  I'm on my way to a meeting.

01:00:24.287 --> 01:00:26.248
Wait! Stop!

01:00:31.837 --> 01:00:35.507
You rejected the idea at the meeting.
Why would you beg someone else to help?

01:00:36.174 --> 01:00:37.175
What…

01:00:38.718 --> 01:00:39.803
Ah.

01:00:40.554 --> 01:00:42.555
I only focus on reality during meetings.

01:00:42.556 --> 01:00:44.765
If I say it's possible
and it turns out it's not,

01:00:44.766 --> 01:00:48.102
the designers will end up
dealing with the consequences.

01:00:48.103 --> 01:00:50.188
You made me seem like an immature kid.

01:00:51.314 --> 01:00:55.193
If I'd known, I wouldn't have gone on
about all that protein fabric.

01:00:56.528 --> 01:01:00.114
It's okay, so you don't have
to go through all that trouble.

01:01:00.115 --> 01:01:02.658
It's really, really fine with me.

01:01:02.659 --> 01:01:06.370
So don't go anywhere pleading for help.

01:01:06.371 --> 01:01:07.789
Why are you…

01:01:09.332 --> 01:01:10.917
always saying you're okay?

01:01:12.419 --> 01:01:14.296
This is why I didn't tell you.

01:01:15.463 --> 01:01:18.216
I knew you'd say you're okay
when you're not.

01:01:20.343 --> 01:01:22.469
It's my job to take care of such issues.

01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:24.806
So you can be greedy about what you want

01:01:26.391 --> 01:01:28.184
and tell people…

01:01:29.227 --> 01:01:30.562
you're not okay

01:01:32.063 --> 01:01:33.064
when you're not.

01:01:40.071 --> 01:01:41.948
What…

01:01:46.953 --> 01:01:51.249
When did I keep saying I was okay?

01:02:03.637 --> 01:02:05.764
Mom…

01:02:17.400 --> 01:02:18.944
I have to be okay.

01:02:20.487 --> 01:02:22.280
I have to keep our family together.

01:02:26.743 --> 01:02:28.203
I have to be okay.

01:02:28.870 --> 01:02:31.373
I have to be okay.

01:02:36.378 --> 01:02:37.587
Mr. Yeon.

01:02:39.464 --> 01:02:40.590
I'm sorry.

01:02:41.967 --> 01:02:43.635
Why are you sorry?

01:02:44.302 --> 01:02:46.096
You're the first one to come here.

01:02:46.680 --> 01:02:49.056
Go and say goodbye to Mom and Dad.

01:02:49.057 --> 01:02:50.058
I'm sorry.

01:02:51.643 --> 01:02:52.769
I'm really sorry.

01:03:02.862 --> 01:03:05.197
I can't believe
I slept for an hour at a restaurant.

01:03:05.198 --> 01:03:06.366
You should've woken me.

01:03:07.075 --> 01:03:10.202
Huh? Wasn't that restaurant your home?

01:03:10.203 --> 01:03:12.496
You slept so comfortably,
I thought it was your house.

01:03:12.497 --> 01:03:15.958
I slept while you're the one
who took a 10-hour flight.

01:03:15.959 --> 01:03:17.793
Go home and get some sleep.

01:03:17.794 --> 01:03:20.004
No, I'm wide awake now.

01:03:20.005 --> 01:03:24.174
But didn't you come from the airport?
Where's all your luggage?

01:03:24.175 --> 01:03:25.384
What luggage?

01:03:26.594 --> 01:03:27.928
My suitcase!

01:03:27.929 --> 01:03:30.390
DEPARTURE TEAM 1

01:03:36.521 --> 01:03:40.107
All your important stuff must be in there.
How could you forget a whole bag?

01:03:40.108 --> 01:03:43.110
I was just in a hurry to make it on time.

01:03:43.111 --> 01:03:44.862
Don't worry.

01:03:44.863 --> 01:03:48.866
The lost and found system's pretty good,
so I'm sure I'll find it.

01:03:48.867 --> 01:03:51.911
Sir, please stop
in front of the coffee-colored gate.

01:03:53.038 --> 01:03:54.329
Tell me when you find it.

01:03:54.330 --> 01:03:57.708
Don't wait up for me.
I'll leave you a message if I find it.

01:03:57.709 --> 01:03:59.669
Uh…

01:04:00.211 --> 01:04:02.963
You might fall asleep in the yard
on the way inside.

01:04:02.964 --> 01:04:06.175
I'll go to SHIM tomorrow morning.

01:04:06.176 --> 01:04:08.636
Okay. I'll see you tomorrow, then.

01:04:14.934 --> 01:04:16.478
What a shame.

01:04:26.154 --> 01:04:29.031
I found it.

01:04:29.032 --> 01:04:31.200
DESIGNER SONG HARAN

01:04:31.201 --> 01:04:32.368
I'll see you tomorrow.

01:04:36.790 --> 01:04:39.750
I told you not to wait up.

01:04:39.751 --> 01:04:42.544
Did you check your stuff?
Is everything inside?

01:04:42.545 --> 01:04:43.546
Yes, I checked…

01:04:51.262 --> 01:04:52.430
That's great.

01:04:58.978 --> 01:05:01.855
Didn't you say you hated the first snow?

01:05:01.856 --> 01:05:03.107
The first snow?

01:05:03.108 --> 01:05:07.945
I did, but I feel like
I'll start hating it less now.

01:05:07.946 --> 01:05:09.030
But why do you ask?

01:05:10.532 --> 01:05:14.451
You said you hated it,
but you're wandering about outside.

01:05:14.452 --> 01:05:16.371
Do you even know where I am?

01:05:17.080 --> 01:05:18.498
Can you see me?

01:05:19.332 --> 01:05:20.333
Where are you?

01:05:20.834 --> 01:05:23.001
You said you were home…

01:05:23.002 --> 01:05:24.712
I thought I'd regret it.

01:05:27.549 --> 01:05:31.761
After you suddenly disappeared,
I had a lot of regrets.

01:05:32.387 --> 01:05:36.723
I kept remembering how harsh
I was on you when you were so nice to me.

01:05:38.768 --> 01:05:43.021
I don't want to have any more regrets,
so can you help me out?

01:05:48.319 --> 01:05:53.241
Is it okay if I be really nice
to you this time?

01:05:59.247 --> 01:06:00.707
I'll start today.

01:06:01.207 --> 01:06:03.626
I'll keep you company on the way to Seoul.

01:06:05.461 --> 01:06:07.797
But where are you?

01:06:09.424 --> 01:06:10.425
I found you.

01:06:19.434 --> 01:06:20.476
This is bad.

01:06:21.895 --> 01:06:23.354
What? What's bad?

01:06:23.938 --> 01:06:26.065
I've been holding back until now…

01:06:27.567 --> 01:06:31.613
I can't even explain myself to you,

01:06:32.739 --> 01:06:36.326
and I shouldn't like you this much.

01:06:37.577 --> 01:06:40.579
- Your bag…
-  I shouldn't keep wanting you…

01:06:40.580 --> 01:06:43.374
- You should bring…
- …like this…

01:07:15.281 --> 01:07:16.448
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:07:40.473 --> 01:07:42.641
He spoke as if he knew me.

01:07:42.642 --> 01:07:47.437
I may not be as good
for Designer Song.

01:07:47.438 --> 01:07:49.231
You used to call him Chan.

01:07:49.232 --> 01:07:52.442
Your old boyfriend, Hyeokchan.

01:07:52.443 --> 01:07:54.696
Their names… were similar.

01:07:55.530 --> 01:07:58.240
How much do you know
about Haran's past?

01:07:58.241 --> 01:08:01.744
I'm sorry for leaving like that
and for hurting you.

01:08:02.495 --> 01:08:04.538
Why is this pen here?

01:08:04.539 --> 01:08:08.000
If I just play dumb
and be greedy until I go back,

01:08:08.001 --> 01:08:10.128
would that be wrong?

01:08:22.390 --> 01:08:23.473
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:08:23.474 --> 01:08:24.475
Translated by Juyoung Park
